# LaTeX build artefacts.
#
# Everything here is regenerable from the .tex sources by pdfLaTeX/BibTeX/latexmk.
# The generated PDFs are ignored too: a committed PDF goes stale silently, and a
# stale manuscript PDF is worse than no PDF. Rebuild rather than commit.
#
# NOT ignored, and must stay tracked: *.tex, references.bib, figures/*.pdf,
# make_figures.py, README.md. The figures are inputs to the build, not outputs of it.

## Core latex/pdflatex
*.aux
*.lof
*.log
*.lot
*.fls
*.out
*.toc
*.fmt
*.fot
*.cb
*.cb2
.*.lb

## Intermediate documents
*.dvi
*.xdv
*-converted-to.*

## Generated PDFs (regenerate; never commit)
main.pdf
supplement.pdf
cover_letter.pdf

## Bibliography (BibTeX / biber)
*.bbl
*.bcf
*.blg
*-blx.aux
*-blx.bib
*.run.xml
*.brf

## Index / glossary / nomenclature
*.idx
*.ilg
*.ind
*.acn
*.acr
*.glg
*.glo
*.gls
*.glsdefs
*.nlo
*.nls

## Cross-referencing and hyperref
*.brf
*.upa
*.upb

## latexmk
*.fdb_latexmk
*.synctex
*.synctex(busy)
*.synctex.gz
*.synctex.gz(busy)
*.pdfsync

## algorithms / listings / todonotes / minted, if ever added
*.alg
*.loa
*.lol
*.tdo
_minted*
*.pyg

## Editor and OS noise
*.swp
*~
.DS_Store
.vscode/
.texpadtmp/
*.sublime-workspace

## Overleaf round-trip leftovers
*.zip
output/
